Third-party software used by this sample

This repository holds none of the packages listed here. `npm install` fetches them, and the build
copies parts of some of them into the page it produces: the code that runs in the browser, and the
font files of @fontsource/fredoka and @fontsource/jetbrains-mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1). The
build puts a copy of this file next to them as THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.

The list covers every package that package-lock.json installs for production: the dependencies in
package.json and everything they depend on, the peer dependencies npm installs by itself, and the
copies bundled inside other packages. This repository's own workspace packages are left out.
`node scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs` writes it, with generate-license-file 4.2.5 for the license
texts, and `node scripts/third-party-licenses.mjs --check` fails when a package is missing. Write it
again when a dependency changes.

